edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186481646 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "ee2dac8c-ea1a-540c-93ab-6f8d5b85be8c" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186481653 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186481580 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186481653 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186481584 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186481653 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186481588 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186481653 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186481634 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186481653 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186481646 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186481653 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186481653 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186481653 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186481588 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186481653 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "287256f7-b082-5a2a-854b-414b7b8a37a2" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186481664 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186481653 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186481664 #edb/ref 1069 "q-162827" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186481664 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186481664 #edb/ref 1071 "| $f$ | $Y=-2$ | $Y=0$ | $Y=2$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=0$ | $0.16$ | $0.09$ | $0.05$ |\n| $X=1$ | $0.44$ | $0.21$ | $0.05$ |\n\nThe joint probability distribution $f(x,y)$ of the discrete random variables $X$ and $Y$ is given above, while the marginal mass functions for these variables are shown below.\n\n<table align=\"center\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<th>\n<table align=\"center\" cellpadding=\"10\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" width=\"30\">$x$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$0$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$1$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" width=\"30\">${f}_{X}(x)$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$0.3$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$0.7$</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<p></p></th>\n<th width=\"50\"></th>\n<th>\n<table align=\"center\" cellpadding=\"10\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" width=\"30\">$y$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$-2$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$0$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$2$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" width=\"30\">${f}_{Y}(y)$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$0.6$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$0.3$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$0.1$</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<p></p></th></tr></tbody></table>\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nI. $P(X=0,Y=0)=P(X=0)\\cdot P(Y=0)$\n\nII. $P(X=x,Y=y)=P(X=x)\\cdot P(Y=y)$ for all possible $x$ and $y$\n\nIII. $X$ and $Y$ are independent" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186481664 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "34f7a331-3a09-5214-b793-a1233bb14dc6" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186481664 #edb/ref 1074 "Two discrete random variables $X$ and $Y$ with a joint probability mass function $f(x,y)$ are independent if and only if \n\n$$\nf(x,y)={f}_{X}(x)\\cdot {f}_{Y}(y)\n$$\n\n \n\nfor all possible values $x$ and $y,$ where ${f}_{X}(x)$ and ${f}_{Y}(y)$ are the marginal probability mass functions for $X$ and $Y,$ respectively.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements.\n\n- Statement I is true. From the table, we obtain that $P(X=0,Y=0)=f(0,0)=0.09.$ On the other hand, \n\n$$\nP(X=0)\\cdot P(Y=0)={f}_{X}(0)\\cdot {f}_{Y}(0)=0.3\\cdot 0.3=0.09.\\,✓\n$$\n\n- Statement II is false. Checking some possible products, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(0,-2) & =0.16\\ne 0.3\\cdot 0.6={f}_{X}(0)\\cdot {f}_{Y}(-2) & \\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, $P(X=x,Y=y)\\ne P(X=x)\\cdot P(Y=y)$ for all possible $x$ and $y.$\n\n- Statement III is false. Since statement II is false, our random variables $X$ and $Y$ are *not* independent.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\"" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186481685 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186481738 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186481685 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "225f3922-71d0-5828-b8ff-8fffbfb93314" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186481685 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186342241 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186481719 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186481733 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186481719 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "8b8b53b4-c35a-5ca7-a8ea-c47534397dd5" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186481719 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186481664 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186481733 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186481746 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186481733 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "cd274b10-c0ca-520e-a49b-be984f15746a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186481733 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186287749 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186481737 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186481748 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186481737 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "d7953f7e-ce6e-54dc-8567-32347c44dc0b" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186481737 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186429817 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186481738 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186481737 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186481738 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "dcc43919-02cb-5986-afb0-91015014e6f6" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186481738 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186398576 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186481746 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "f541f3e5-d2a5-58a4-bb6b-ba161c260278" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186481746 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186429818 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186481748 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186481719 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186481748 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "f7fcb20d-433e-5fe0-9143-ce6e7eaa5c1a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186481748 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186115884 #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
